  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday morning through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 149 PM EDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nTemperatures during the daytime will climb into the low to mid 70s \nacross most of the CWA before we see some low 80s as we go into the \nweekend as the winds swing around to the south. High pressure begins \nto break down with the approach of a trough from the west and we'll \nsee the chances of showers and possibly a thunderstorm start to \nincrease late on Saturday evening before sweeping through on Sunday. \nWhile the threat of severe weather is marginal, the GFS shows a \ndecent amount of rain on Sunday with values ranging from 1.5-2.5\". \n\nOn the flip side of that, the Euro keeps rainfall totals at less \nthan half an inch, coming in with a significantly drier solution. \nRegardless of how it plays out, current drought conditions should \nminimalize the overall flood threat. Some localized flash \nflooding will be possible if the GFS gets it right with training \nstorms and in the metro area. \n\nThe system will clear out late Sunday, giving us a few more days of \nclear fall weather. Another round of rain and possibly a \nthunderstorm will creep it's way back into the forecast towards the \nmiddle of next work week.",
